Performance: Gates

Purpose:
  Defines performance gates including load testing and resilience checks.

GateSchema:
  Format: PERFORMANCE-GATE-<ID>
  Condition: <performance criterion>
  Evidence: <performance report>
  Threshold: <pass/fail criteria>
  Owner: QA/DevOps
  Decision: PASS / FAIL

GateTypes:
  Load:
    Condition: System handles expected load
    Metrics: RPS, P50, P95, P99, Error rate, CPU, Memory, DB latency, Cache hit rate, Queue latency
    Threshold: Context-dependent
  Resilience:
    Condition: System withstands load/resilience simulation
    Checks: Rate limiting, WAF, CDN, Load balancer, Autoscaling
    Note: Agent creates controlled test plan, does not execute real attacks.

Rules:
  [PF1] Load testing is context-dependent (not all projects need it).
  [PF2] Resilience gate uses controlled simulation, not real attacks.
  [PF3] Performance thresholds are based on project scale.
  [PF4] Performance gate failure blocks release for L3+.

State: +
